PS C:\Users\baira\OneDrive\Documents\AI_Projects\payment-system\payment-servi","selectedFiles":[],"agentId":null,"correlationId":null,"id":"40af105b-dd1b-448d-8413-2cfad038b3fc","promptLibrary":null,"response":"• **Database mismatch**: Application connects to PostgreSQL instead of MySQL despite configuration
• **Missing table**: Hibernate expects `payments` table but it doesn't exist in the database
• **Invalid Spring Boot version**: Still using non-existent version 4.0.0 causing compatibility issues

## Root Cause Analysis

The logs show three critical issues:
1. PostgreSQL connection (`org.postgresql.jdbc.PgConnection`) despite MySQL configuration
2. Missing `payments` table causing schema validation failure
3. Spring Boot 4.0.0 version which doesn't exist

## Complete Solution

**Fixed POM Configuration**

```xml::pom.xml::payment-service/pom.xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
