```markdown::exception-handling.md::docs/architecture/exception-handling.md
# Payment System - Exception Handling Architecture

## Exception Hierarchy

	```plantuml
	@startuml Exception Hierarchy
	!theme plain

	abstract class PaymentSystemException {
	  - errorCode: String
	  - message: String
	  - details: Map<String,Object>
	  + getHttpStatus(): HttpStatus
	}

	class PaymentNotFoundException {
	  - paymentId: String
	  + getHttpStatus(): 404
	}

	class InvalidPaymentStateException {
	  - currentState: PaymentStatus
	  - requestedState: PaymentStatus
	  + getHttpStatus(): 409
	}

	class PaymentProcessingException {
	  - reason: String
	  + getHttpStatus(): 500
	}

	class PaymentValidationException {
	  - violations: List<String>
	  + getHttpStatus(): 400
	}

	class ExternalServiceException {
	  - serviceName: String
	  - originalError: String
	  + getHttpStatus(): 503
	}

	PaymentSystemException <|-- PaymentNotFoundException
	PaymentSystemException <|-- InvalidPaymentStateException
	PaymentSystemException <|-- PaymentProcessingException
	PaymentSystemException <|-- PaymentValidationException
	PaymentSystemException <|-- ExternalServiceException

	@enduml
	```

## Global Exception Handler

	```java
	@RestControllerAdvice
	public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

	    @ExceptionHandler(PaymentNotFoundException.class)
	    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleNotFound(PaymentNotFoundException ex) {
	        ErrorResponse error = ErrorResponse.builder()
	            .code("PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND")
	            .message(ex.getMessage())
	            .timestamp(LocalDateTime.now())
	            .path(getPath())
	            .build();
	        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body(error);
	    }

	    @ExceptionHandler(InvalidPaymentStateException.class)
	    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleInvalidState(InvalidPaymentStateException ex) {
	        ErrorResponse error = ErrorResponse.builder()
	            .code("INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION")
	            .message(ex.getMessage())
	            .details(Map.of(
	                "currentState", ex.getCurrentState(),
	                "requestedState", ex.getRequestedState()
	            ))
	            .timestamp(LocalDateTime.now())
	            .build();
	        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CONFLICT).body(error);
	    }

	    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)
	    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleValidation(MethodArgumentNotValidException ex) {
	        List<String> errors = ex.getBindingResult()
	            .getFieldErrors()
	            .stream()
	            .map(error -> error.getField() + ": " + error.getDefaultMessage())
	            .collect(Collectors.toList());

	        ErrorResponse error = ErrorResponse.builder()
	            .code("VALIDATION_FAILED")
	            .message("Request validation failed")
	            .details(Map.of("violations", errors))
	            .timestamp(LocalDateTime.now())
	            .build();
	        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST).body(error);
	    }

	    @ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)
	    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleGeneric(Exception ex) {
	        log.error("Unexpected error", ex);
	        ErrorResponse error = ErrorResponse.builder()
	            .code("INTERNAL_ERROR")
	            .message("An unexpected error occurred")
	            .timestamp(LocalDateTime.now())
	            .build();
	        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR).body(error);
	    }
	}
	```

## Error Response Format

	```json
	{
	  "code": "PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND",
	  "message": "Payment with ID 12345 not found",
	  "timestamp": "2024-01-01T10:00:00",
	  "path": "/api/payments/12345",
	  "details": {
	    "paymentId": "12345"
	  }
	}
	```

## Exception Handling Strategies

### 1. Service Layer
- Catch and wrap external exceptions
- Add context to exceptions
- Log with appropriate levels
- Maintain transaction integrity

### 2. Repository Layer
- Handle database exceptions
- Convert to domain exceptions
- Retry transient failures

### 3. Event Publishing
- Async error handling
- Dead letter queue for failures
- Retry with exponential backoff

### 4. Batch Processing
- Continue on individual failures
- Aggregate error reporting
- Checkpoint and resume capability

## Monitoring and Alerting

### Error Metrics
- Exception count by type
- Error rate per endpoint
- Response time during errors
- Circuit breaker status

### Logging Strategy
- Structured error logging
- Correlation ID tracking
- Stack trace management
- PII data masking
```

```markdown::security-architecture.md::docs/architecture/security-architecture.md
# Payment System - Security Architecture

## Security Layers

	```plantuml
	@startuml Security Architecture
	!theme plain

	package "External Layer" {
	  [API Gateway/WAF]
	  [TLS Termination]
	  [Rate Limiting]
	}

	package "Application Layer" {
	  [Authentication Filter]
	  [Authorization]
	  [Input Validation]
	  [CORS Policy]
	}

	package "Service Layer" {
	  [Business Logic Security]
	  [Transaction Security]
	  [Audit Logging]
	}

	package "Data Layer" {
	  [Encryption at Rest]
	  [Database Access Control]
	  [Data Masking]
	}

	package "Infrastructure Layer" {
	  [Network Segmentation]
	  [Secret Management]
	  [Container Security]
	}

	[API Gateway/WAF] --> [Authentication Filter]
	[Authentication Filter] --> [Authorization]
	[Authorization] --> [Business Logic Security]
	[Business Logic Security] --> [Database Access Control]

	@enduml
	```

## Security Controls

### 1. Authentication & Authorization
	```java
	@Configuration
	@EnableWebSecurity
	public class SecurityConfig {

	    @Bean
	    public SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
	        return http
	            .csrf().disable()
	            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
	                .requestMatchers("/health/**").permitAll()
	                .requestMatchers("/api/payments/**").authenticated()
	                .anyRequest().denyAll()
	            )
	            .addFilterBefore(new JwtAuthenticationFilter(), UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter.class)
	            .sessionManagement().sessionCreationPolicy(SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS)
	            .build();
	    }
	}
	```

### 2. Input Validation
	```java
	@Component
	public class PaymentValidator {

	    public void validatePaymentRequest(PaymentRequest request) {
	        // Amount validation
	        if (request.getAmount().compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) <= 0) {
	            throw new PaymentValidationException("Amount must be positive");
	        }

	        // SQL injection prevention
	        if (containsSqlKeywords(request.getDescription())) {
	            throw new PaymentValidationException("Invalid characters in description");
	        }

	        // XSS prevention
	        String sanitized = Jsoup.clean(request.getDescription(), Whitelist.none());
	        if (!sanitized.equals(request.getDescription())) {
	            throw new PaymentValidationException("Invalid HTML content");
	        }
	    }
	}
	```

### 3. Data Protection
- **Encryption at Rest**: AES-256 for sensitive fields
- **Encryption in Transit**: TLS 1.3 minimum
- **Data Masking**: PII fields in logs
- **Tokenization**: Payment card data

### 4. Audit Logging
	```java
	@Aspect
	@Component
	public class AuditAspect {

	    @Around("@annotation(Auditable)")
	    public Object audit(ProceedingJoinPoint joinPoint) throws Throwable {
	        AuditEvent event = AuditEvent.builder()
	            .userId(SecurityContext.getCurrentUser())
	            .action(joinPoint.getSignature().getName())
	            .resource("Payment")
	            .timestamp(LocalDateTime.now())
	            .build();

	        try {
	            Object result = joinPoint.proceed();
	            event.setStatus("SUCCESS");
	            return result;
	        } catch (Exception e) {
	            event.setStatus("FAILURE");
	            event.setReason(e.getMessage());
	            throw e;
	        } finally {
	            auditLogger.log(event);
	        }
	    }
	}
	```

### 5. Secret Management
- Environment variables for credentials
- Vault integration for sensitive data
- Regular key rotation
- No hardcoded secrets

### 6. API Security
- Rate limiting per client
- API key management
- Request signing
- Replay attack prevention

### 7. Container Security
- Non-root user execution
- Read-only file systems
- Security scanning in CI/CD
- Minimal base images

## Security Monitoring

### Real-time Alerts
- Failed authentication attempts
- Unusual transaction patterns
- Rate limit violations
- Security exception spikes

### Security Metrics
- Authentication success/failure rates
- API endpoint access patterns
- Security exception counts
- Vulnerability scan results

## Compliance Requirements

### PCI DSS
- Secure payment data handling
- Network segmentation
- Access control
- Regular security assessments

### GDPR
- Data privacy controls
- Right to erasure
- Data portability
- Consent management

### Security Testing
- SAST/DAST integration
- Penetration testing
- Security code reviews
- Dependency scanning
```

