```bash
mvn clean install
```

```bash
java -jar target/payment-batch-job.jar
```

Expected: Application starts without `ClassNotFoundException` for `LogstashEncoder`.

## Explanation

The error occurs because the [logback-spring.xml](payment-batch-job/src/main/resources/logback-spring.xml) configuration references `net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder` but the corresponding JAR is missing from the classpath. Adding the `logstash-logback-encoder` dependency version 8.0 (compatible with Spring Boot 3.x) provides the required encoder classes for structured JSON logging, enabling integration with centralized logging systems like ELK stack.






