## Explanation

The compile errors were caused by mixing incompatible Prometheus client library versions. The old `simpleclient_pushgateway` doesn't work well with the new Micrometer Prometheus registry in Spring Boot 3.x. The solution uses the native HTTP client to push metrics directly to the Pushgateway using the standard Prometheus exposition format, which is more reliable and doesn't require additional Prometheus client dependencies. The configuration now properly integrates with Spring Boot's metrics system and provides both shutdown and scheduled metric pushing capabilities.






