## Explanation

The error occurs because the [logback-spring.xml](payment-batch-job/src/main/resources/logback-spring.xml) configuration file references `net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder` but the corresponding JAR is missing from the classpath. Adding the `logstash-logback-encoder` dependency version 8.0 (compatible with Spring Boot 3.x) resolves this by providing the required encoder classes for structured JSON logging. This dependency enables the application to use Logstash-compatible JSON format for logs, which is essential for centralized logging systems like ELK stack.






